WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.930
We present a wearable,
motion capture system

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:10.030
that can acquire
emotions of an individual

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:12.520
almost anywhere over
extended periods of time.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.910
Our system consists of an array
of small, low-cost, low-power

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:18.280
sensors placed on
the body of a person.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.290
The system is
completely autonomous.

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:24.190
It does not require any external
devices or signal sources.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.460
In this prototype, we use eight
signal sources and 18 signal

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.130
detectors as our
sensors, our sources

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.020
are small, ultrasonic
transducers

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.250
that sequentially emit pulses
about 16 times a second each.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:38.530
We use small microphones
as signal detectors

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.390
for the ultrasonic pulses.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:43.480
The detectors also contain
three-axis accelerometers

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.450
and three-axis gyroscopes
that sample accelerations

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.930
and angular velocities
about 140 times per second,

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:52.690
significantly improving the
precision and the frame rate

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.370
of the ultrasonic measurements.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:56.230
Using the onboard
microprocessor,

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:58.150
the accelerometer
and gyro values

00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:59.890
are digitally
encoded and combined

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:03.130
with the analog audio
signal from the microphones.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:06.700
All signal sources and detectors
are wired to the driver box.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:09.920
The driver box consists of
the following components--

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.210
18 second-stage amplifiers
that further amplify the signal

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:17.470
from each of the sensors, 3
six-channel, analog-to-digital

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:20.350
converters that sample
the signal from 18 sensors

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:25.180
at 150 kilosamples per
second, a microcontroller that

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:28.180
synchronizes all HD
converters and generates pulse

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:31.200
signals for the
ultrasonic transducers.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.860
The signal from
the microcontroller

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.170
to the transducers
is then amplified

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:37.270
by the transducer drivers.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:39.970
The driver box is powered by
a small, rechargeable battery

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:42.400
pack that lasts for
more than four hours.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.290
The data from all
A-to-D converters

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:47.050
is transmitted using
a USB 2.0 connection

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:49.390
to a laptop which records
this data directly

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:50.650
to its hard drive.

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:54.160
The driver box and laptop can
be carried in a small backpack.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:57.070
Our prototype system was built
from off-the-shelf components

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:01.170
for less than $3,000.

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:03.510
Here is a comparison
between our reconstruction

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.400
and that of the
Vicon optical system.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.620
In this sequence,
distance measurements

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:32.270
prevent drift in
the left shoulder.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:50.450
The mobility of
our system allows

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.970
us to capture motion virtually
anywhere, for example,

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.020
while driving a car.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.730
We were able to track all
limbs as well as recover more

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:24.095
detailed and subtle motions.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.220
Even motions that are
traditionally hard to acquire

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:23.389
are captured with
ease using our system.

